/-!
# The blowup of an affine scheme in a finitely generated ideal, inside projective space

Let `R` be a commutative ring and let `I ⊆ R` be generated by `x₀, …, x_{m-1}`. Placing the
generators in degree one presents the Rees algebra `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ` as a graded quotient of the
polynomial ring `R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]`, so the blowup of `Spec R` in `I`, which is `Proj` of the
Rees algebra, is a closed subscheme of `Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] = 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}`, by a closed
immersion over `Spec R`.

For a regular local ring of dimension two the maximal ideal is generated by two elements, so the
blowup of such a ring in its maximal ideal is a closed subscheme of the projective line over the
base. That is the closed immersion of Stacks tag 0AGQ.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesPresentation`: the graded homomorphism `R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] ⟶ ⨁ₙ Iⁿ`
  attached to a family `x₀, …, x_{m-1}` of elements of `I`, sending `Tᵢ` to `xᵢ` in degree one.
* `Stacks.Blowup.projSpaceToSpec`: the structure morphism `Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] ⟶ Spec R`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpace`: the induced morphism from the blowup of `Spec R` in `I`
  to `Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.surjective_gradedAddHom_reesPresentation` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.surjective_reesPresentation`: the presentation is surjective, in every degree
  and globally, as soon as the family generates the ideal.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpecToProjSpace`: the induced morphism is a closed
  immersion.
* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpace_comp_projSpaceToSpec`: it is a morphism over `Spec R`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_range_eq_maximalIdeal`: the maximal ideal of a regular local ring of
  dimension two is generated by two elements.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpec_maximalIdeal`: the blowup of a regular
  local ring of dimension two in its maximal ideal is a closed subscheme of the projective line
  over the base, over the base.

## Implementation notes

The projective line over `Spec R` is presented as `Proj R[T₀, T₁]`, which is the presentation the
source itself uses (`𝐏¹_S = Proj(A[T₀, T₁])`) and the one under which the twisting sheaves of
Stacks tag 01MN are available; it is also the presentation
`AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveLineProj` uses over a field. The pullback model
`AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveSpaceOverRing` is not used, because no isomorphism between the two
models over a general coefficient ring is available.

Degreewise surjectivity of the presentation is Mathlib's
`Ideal.mem_span_pow_iff_exists_isHomogeneous`: an element of `Iⁿ` is the value at `x` of a
homogeneous polynomial of degree `n`. Global surjectivity is then assembled from the homogeneous
decomposition of the Rees algebra. Surjectivity, not merely surjectivity in large degrees,
is what both `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.irrelevant_le_map_of_surjective` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_of_surjective` consume.

`Stacks.Blowup.toSpec` writes the structure morphism of the blowup as `Proj.toSpecZero` followed
by `Spec` of the identification of the degree-zero part of the Rees algebra with `R`, and
`Stacks.Blowup.projSpaceToSpec` is written the same way with
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.gradeZeroEquiv` in place of
`Stacks.Blowup.reesGradingZeroEquiv`. The square over the base is then
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_toSpecZero` together with the computation
`Stacks.Blowup.gradedZeroRingHom_reesPresentation_comp_gradeZeroEquiv`, which says that both
identifications are `algebraMap` from `R` and that the presentation sends a constant polynomial
to the corresponding element of the Rees algebra.

`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec` is a plain definition rather than an abbreviation, so a rewrite whose
left-hand side mentions `Proj (reesGrading I)` does not fire against it; the square over the base
is therefore proved in the `Proj` spelling and transported by `exact`.

The grading of a polynomial ring by total degree is a local instance, as elsewhere in the
library, because a polynomial ring carries several useful gradings.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Polynomial

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

/-- A monomial of weighted degree `n` for the all-ones weight has exponents summing to `n`. -/
private theorem sum_support_eq_of_weight_one {m n : ℕ} {d : Fin m →₀ ℕ}
    (hd : Finsupp.weight (1 : Fin m → ℕ) d = n) : ∑ i ∈ d.support, d i = n := by
  simpa [Finsupp.weight, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, Finsupp.sum] using hd

/-- Evaluating a homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` at degree-one elements of a graded ring,
with the coefficients sent to degree zero, lands in the degree-`n` part. -/
theorem eval₂Hom_mem_of_isHomogeneous {S T σ : Type*} [CommRing S] [CommRing T] [SetLike σ T]
    [AddSubmonoidClass σ T] (D : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing D] (f : S →+* T) {m : ℕ} (g : Fin m → T)
    (hf : ∀ r, f r ∈ D 0) (hg : ∀ i, g i ∈ D 1) {p : MvPolynomial (Fin m) S} {n : ℕ}
    (hp : p.IsHomogeneous n) : MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f g p ∈ D n := by
  classical
  have hpow : ∀ (i : Fin m) (e : ℕ), g i ^ e ∈ D e := by
    intro i e
    induction e with
    | zero => simpa using SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := D)
    | succ e he => simpa [pow_succ] using SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem he (hg i)
  have hprod : ∀ (d : Fin m →₀ ℕ) (s : Finset (Fin m)),
      (∏ i ∈ s, g i ^ d i) ∈ D (∑ i ∈ s, d i) := by
    intro d s
    induction s using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty => simpa using SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := D)
    | insert i s his ih =>
        rw [Finset.prod_insert his, Finset.sum_insert his]
        exact SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem (hpow i (d i)) ih
  change MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous (1 : Fin m → ℕ) p n at hp
  induction hp using MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add p q hp hq ihp ihq => simpa [map_add] using add_mem ihp ihq
  | monomial d r hd =>
      rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_monomial]
      simpa [sum_support_eq_of_weight_one hd, Finsupp.prod] using
        SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem (hf r) (hprod d d.support)

/-- The polynomial ring `R[x₀, …, xₘ₋₁]` is graded by total degree, with homogeneous
components `MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R`. -/
local instance instGradedAlgebraMvPolynomialFin (m : ℕ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] :
    GradedAlgebra (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) :=
  MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- Evaluating a homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` at the one-variable polynomials `xᵢ X`
produces `Xⁿ` times the value at `x`. -/
private lemma eval₂_C_mul_X_eq_monomial {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) {p : MvPolynomial (Fin m) R}
    {n : ℕ} (hp : p.IsHomogeneous n) :
    MvPolynomial.eval₂ (C : R →+* R[X]) (fun i ↦ C (x i) * X) p =
      (monomial n) (MvPolynomial.eval x p) := by
  classical
  change MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous (1 : Fin m → ℕ) p n at hp
  induction hp using MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add p q hp hq ihp ihq => simp [ihp, ihq]
  | monomial d r hd =>
      rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂_monomial, MvPolynomial.eval_monomial,
        ← sum_support_eq_of_weight_one hd, Finsupp.prod,
        Finsupp.prod, ← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, map_mul, map_prod]
      simp only [map_pow, mul_pow, Finset.prod_mul_distrib, Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum]
      ring

variable (I : Ideal R)

/-! ### The polynomial presentation of a Rees algebra -/

/-- **The polynomial presentation of a Rees algebra.** A family `x : Fin m → R` of elements of
`I` determines a homomorphism of graded rings `R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] ⟶ ⨁ₙ Iⁿ` sending `Tᵢ` to `xᵢ`
in degree one. -/
@[sga "6 VII 3.5" "partial"]
def reesPresentation {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) :
    MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R →+*ᵍ reesGrading I where
  toRingHom := MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I))
    (fun i ↦ (reesMonomial I 1 ⟨x i, by simpa using hx i⟩ : reesAlgebra I))
  map_mem {n p} hp := eval₂Hom_mem_of_isHomogeneous (reesGrading I) _ _
    (fun r ↦ SetLike.algebraMap_mem_graded _ r) (fun i ↦ (reesMonomial I 1 _).2) hp

/-- The polynomial presentation of a Rees algebra, composed with the inclusion of the Rees
algebra into `R[X]`, is the evaluation sending `Tᵢ` to `xᵢ X`. -/
theorem val_comp_reesPresentation {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) :
    (reesAlgebra I).val.toRingHom.comp (reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom =
      MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (C : R →+* R[X]) (fun i ↦ C (x i) * X) := by
  refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun a ↦ ?_) (fun i ↦ ?_)
  · have h1 : (reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C a) =
        algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) a := MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C _ _ a
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, h1, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C]
    change ((algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) a : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = C a
    simp
  · have h2 : (reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X i) =
        (reesMonomial I 1 ⟨x i, by simpa using hx i⟩ : reesAlgebra I) :=
      MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ i
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, h2, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X']
    change ((reesMonomial I 1 ⟨x i, by simpa using hx i⟩ : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = C (x i) * X
    rw [coe_reesMonomial, ← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial]
    simp

/-- The polynomial presentation of a Rees algebra, read inside `R[X]`: a homogeneous polynomial
of degree `n` is sent to `Xⁿ` times its value at `x`. -/
theorem coe_reesPresentation_apply {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    {p : MvPolynomial (Fin m) R} {n : ℕ} (hp : p.IsHomogeneous n) :
    ((reesPresentation I x hx p : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) =
      (monomial n) (MvPolynomial.eval x p) := by
  rw [← eval₂_C_mul_X_eq_monomial x hp]
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun (val_comp_reesPresentation I x hx) p

/-- **The polynomial presentation is surjective in every degree** as soon as the family
generates the ideal: an element of `Iⁿ` is the value at `x` of a homogeneous polynomial of
degree `n`. -/
@[sga "6 VII 3.5" "Surjectivity of O_X[T_1"]
theorem surjective_gradedAddHom_reesPresentation {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom (reesPresentation I x hx) n) := by
  intro b
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ : ∃ r : (I ^ n : Ideal R), reesGradingEquivPow I n r = b :=
    ⟨(reesGradingEquivPow I n).symm b, (reesGradingEquivPow I n).apply_symm_apply b⟩
  have hmem : (r : R) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range x) ^ n := by rw [← hspan]; exact r.2
  obtain ⟨p, hp, heval⟩ := (Ideal.mem_span_pow_iff_exists_isHomogeneous x (r : R)).1 hmem
  refine ⟨⟨p, hp⟩, Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext ?_)⟩
  rw [← hr, coe_reesGradingEquivPow]
  change ((reesPresentation I x hx p : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = _
  rw [coe_reesPresentation_apply I x hx hp, heval]

/-- **The polynomial presentation is surjective** as soon as the family generates the ideal. -/
theorem surjective_reesPresentation {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    Function.Surjective (reesPresentation I x hx) := by
  classical
  intro y
  choose g hg using fun n : ℕ ↦ surjective_gradedAddHom_reesPresentation I x hx hspan n
    (DirectSum.decompose (reesGrading I) y n)
  refine ⟨∑ n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose (reesGrading I) y).support,
    ((g n : MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R n) : MvPolynomial (Fin m) R), ?_⟩
  rw [map_sum]
  exact (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ ↦ congrArg Subtype.val (hg n)).trans
    (DirectSum.sum_support_decompose (reesGrading I) y)

/-! ### The closed immersion into projective space -/

/-- The structure morphism of `Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]` over `Spec R`: the canonical morphism to
the spectrum of the degree-zero part, followed by the identification of that part with `R`. -/
def projSpaceToSpec (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (m : ℕ) :
    Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R) :=
  Proj.toSpecZero (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) ≫
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.gradeZeroEquiv (Fin m) R).toRingHom)

/-- The polynomial presentation of a Rees algebra is the identity on the coefficient ring: both
degree-zero parts are copies of `R`, through `algebraMap`, and a constant polynomial is sent to
the corresponding element of the Rees algebra. -/
theorem gradedZeroRingHom_reesPresentation_comp_gradeZeroEquiv {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) :
    (reesPresentation I x hx).gradedZeroRingHom.comp
        (AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.gradeZeroEquiv (Fin m) R).toRingHom =
      (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun r ↦ Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext ?_)
  have hsrc : ((AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.gradeZeroEquiv (Fin m) R r :
        MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R 0) : MvPolynomial (Fin m) R) =
      MvPolynomial.C r := by
    change ((algebraMap R (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R 0) r :
      MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R 0) : MvPolynomial (Fin m) R) = MvPolynomial.C r
    simp
  have htgt : (((reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom r : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) =
      algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r :=
    SetLike.GradeZero.coe_algebraMap (reesGrading I) r
  have hpres : (reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C r) =
      algebraMap R (reesAlgebra I) r := MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C _ _ r
  change (((reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.gradeZeroEquiv (Fin m) R r :
      MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R 0) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin m) R) : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = _
  rw [hsrc, hpres, htgt]

/-- **The blowup in an ideal generated by `m` elements maps to `𝐏^{m-1}`.** The polynomial
presentation of the Rees algebra attached to a generating family `x₀, …, x_{m-1}` of `I` induces
a morphism from the blowup of `Spec R` in `I` to `Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]`. -/
@[ega "IV 19.4.11" "(i), special case"]
def blowUpSpecToProjSpace {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    blowUpSpec I ⟶ Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) :=
  Proj.map (reesPresentation I x hx) (Proj.irrelevant_le_map_of_surjective _
    (surjective_reesPresentation I x hx hspan))

/-- **The blowup in an ideal generated by `m` elements is a closed subscheme of `𝐏^{m-1}`.**
The morphism attached to a generating family is a closed immersion, because the polynomial
presentation of the Rees algebra is surjective. -/
@[ega "IV 19.4.11" "(i), special case", sga "6 VII 1.8" "Affine, special case"]
instance isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpecToProjSpace {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    IsClosedImmersion (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan) :=
  Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_of_surjective _ (surjective_reesPresentation I x hx hspan)

/-- **The immersion of the blowup into projective space is a morphism over the base.** -/
theorem blowUpSpecToProjSpace_comp_projSpaceToSpec {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan ≫ projSpaceToSpec R m = toSpec I := by
  have key : Proj.map (reesPresentation I x hx) (Proj.irrelevant_le_map_of_surjective _
        (surjective_reesPresentation I x hx hspan)) ≫ projSpaceToSpec R m =
      Proj.toSpecZero (reesGrading I) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom) := by
    rw [projSpaceToSpec, Proj.map_toSpecZero_assoc, ← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp,
      gradedZeroRingHom_reesPresentation_comp_gradeZeroEquiv I x hx]
  exact key

/-! ### The blowup of a regular local surface -/

/-- **The maximal ideal of a regular local ring of dimension two is generated by two
elements.** -/
theorem exists_range_eq_maximalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) :
    ∃ x : Fin 2 → A, IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hcard, hspan⟩ :=
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)).exists_span_finset_card_eq_spanFinrank
  have hfr : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank = 2 := by
    have h := IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := A)
    rw [hdim] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hcard2 : s.card = 2 := hcard.trans hfr
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ ((s.equivFinOfCardEq hcard2).symm i : A), ?_⟩
  rw [← hspan]
  congr 1
  refine Set.ext fun a ↦ ⟨fun ha ↦ ?_, fun ha ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact ⟨s.equivFinOfCardEq hcard2 ⟨a, Finset.mem_coe.mp ha⟩, by simp⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := ha
    exact ((s.equivFinOfCardEq hcard2).symm i).2

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ.** Let `A` be a regular local ring of dimension two and let
`X ⟶ Spec A` be the blowup of `Spec A` in its maximal ideal. There is a closed immersion
`r : X ⟶ 𝐏¹_{Spec A}` over `Spec A`.

The projective line over `Spec A` is `Proj A[T₀, T₁]`, the presentation the source uses. -/
@[stacks 0AGQ "the closed immersion of the blowup into the projective line over the base"]
theorem exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpec_maximalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) :
    ∃ r : blowUpSpec (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ⟶
        Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) A),
      IsClosedImmersion r ∧
        r ≫ projSpaceToSpec A 2 = toSpec (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hspan⟩ := exists_range_eq_maximalIdeal A hdim
  have hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := fun i ↦ by
    rw [hspan]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨blowUpSpecToProjSpace _ x hx hspan, inferInstance,
    blowUpSpecToProjSpace_comp_projSpaceToSpec _ x hx hspan⟩

end Stacks.Blowup

end
